  "note": "Annual election of the Newtownards Urban Council, January 1928. One seat was vacant in each of the five wards. Castle and Scrabo were both contested at nomination, but by polling day the only contest was in Scrabo Ward; W. M'Alpine was returned unopposed for Castle Ward. Printed: register 784, 588 votes recorded, two papers spoiled. Mr. H. M'Cartney acted as returning officer."
